From deee84e0108d098808f5aa447be91a0a0978d2ba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matthew Schwartz <matthew.schwartz@linux.dev>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 00:10:48 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] steamcompmgr: snapshot the upscale sharpness per frame

The RCAS and NIS passes read the sharpness slider global mid-paint, so
a slider write from another thread lands on whichever frame is being
composited rather than on the one decided with it.

Carry the sharpness in the per-focus upscale settings and read it from
the frame. Cached pre-emptive upscales keep the sharpness they were
made with until the next commit replaces them. Invalidating them would
drop the frame to the live composite, which does not match the
forwarded texture on backends without scanout color management.
