Subject: [PATCH 5/8] mangoapp: report the selected and active upscale filter

mangoapp only learns whether FSR upscaled the base layer, so NIS and
SGSR show as FSR OFF in the overlay while they run every frame, and the
row cannot say which filter the user selected when it is not engaging.

Send gamescope's own filter values rather than a second numbering,
since Steam already writes these to the scaling atom. Older mangoapps
read the two extra bytes into their buffer and ignore them, and a
matching mangoapp change shows them. A cached FSR upscale now counts as
active only while its texture is the one on screen.
